<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jama Masjid, Jaunpur</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1470</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Jama Masjid of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jaunpur">Jaunpur</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uttar-pradesh">Uttar Pradesh</a>, is the largest mosque built by the Sharqi sultans of Jaunpur. Begun in the 1430s and completed around 1470 under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/husain-shah-sharqi">Husain Shah Sharqi</a>, it stands on a raised platform and has a towering arched gateway screen before its domed prayer hall, a defining feature of the Sharqi style.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jama-masjid-jaunpur.jpg" alt="Jama Masjid, Jaunpur" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Varun Shiv Kapur from Berkeley, United States · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Main_arcade_facade,_Jama_Masjid,_Jaunpur.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
